{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789834000,"nonce":"i5rl+pdnrTCBp4IHg8t0hHFbIkM=","title":"a default argument that names a preceding parameter or `this` reads nothing at the call site","message":"Defaults are filled at the call site by lowering the callee's default expression there (`fill_default_args`). `fSibling(a:Int, b:Int = a)` called as `fSibling(5)` lowered `a` -- the callee's parameter symbol -- in the caller, where it is unbound: `b` came out 0 (TestDefaultArgs: `10 != 5`, `1,1,1 != 1,10,0`). `mThis(x:Int = this.instanceField)` read the caller's `this`.\n\nFix: `function_param_symbols` records each defaulted function's parameter symbols next to its defaults; while a default lowers, the earlier parameters map to the arguments already in place (a method's list leaves `this` out, so it sits one before; a constructor's list starts with it) and SymbolId(0) -- how `this` lowers -- maps to the receiver, then the bindings are restored.\n\nStill open in TestDefaultArgs: `Helper.counter` read from the test class stays 0 while `Helper.make()` increments it -- a static of a private class in the same module has two homes.","files":null}]}